Panel scrollHeight 405, client 252, needs 153 more. To fit, we'd need to cut 153px. Options: hide desc (48+7), shrink title (82 -> maybe 55), stat grid 47, ability 126. Could make the ability preview a horizontal 3-column grid with short names only, reducing from 126 to ~40. Stats 47. Title 55. Desc 0. Then total: title 55 + stat 47 + ability 45 + button 42 + margins ~20 = 209, fits. That's doable for short landscape. But ability-preview-row is flex column; we can set `.ability-preview { flex-direction: row; }` and each row flex:1, hide description span already shown; at short landscape, `.ability-preview-row span` currently display:block (short desc), hide it to save height. Set `.ability-preview-row { flex-direction: column; align-items:flex-start; gap:0.15rem; }`? Actually row is flex align center, glyph + text. Horizontal 3 columns: each row width ~ (340-...)/3 ~ 100px, glyph 27 + text; names may wrap. Could hide glyph too or make glyph smaller. Simpler: make `.ability-preview` grid 3 columns, `.ability-preview-row` block with glyph hidden, b font 0.55rem, span hidden. Height ~28. Good.

Also `.select-class-title` 82.6: includes h2, p, role chip? It's block with padding-bottom 0.8rem. Could make flex baseline like portrait: role chip hidden, h2 1.1rem, p inline. Height ~35. Save 47.

Then total: 35 + stat 47 + ability 28 + button 42 + gaps ~20 = 172. Fits easily.

Let's implement short-landscape compaction and the portrait grid fix.

Also need test shop equip flow, defeat result, HUD lobby button, map interactions, other classes/maps. But before that, fix layout and re-test.

Let's patch CSS:
1. In @media max-width 760: `.select-panel { grid-template-columns: minmax(0,1fr) auto; }` and add `.select-panel > * { min-width: 0; }` maybe. Also `.select-panel .btn { min-width: 0; }`.
2. In short landscape: compact select panel:
```
.select-panel { max-height: calc(100dvh - 3.8rem - var(--safe-t) - var(--safe-b)); ... }
.select-class-title { display:flex; align-items:baseline; gap:.5rem; padding-bottom:.35rem; }
.select-class-title h2 { font-size:1.1rem; margin:0; }
.select-class-title p { font-size:.5rem; }
.select-class-title .role-chip { display:none; }
.select-desc { display:none; }
.stat-grid { margin-bottom:.35rem; gap:.2rem .6rem; }
.ability-preview { display:grid; grid-template-columns:repeat(3,minmax(0,1fr)); gap:.3rem; margin-bottom:.4rem; }
.ability-preview-row { display:block; padding:.25rem .3rem; }
.ability-preview-row .ability-glyph { display:none; }
.ability-preview-row span { display:none; }
.ability-preview-row b { font-size:.52rem; }
.select-panel .btn { padding:.45rem; font-size:.58rem; }
```
Also the class cards: at landscape height 390, cards 118.9 tall, row2 remaining height 390 - 8 - 36 - gap etc = ~330, align-self end so cards at bottom 263-382. Fine. Panel starts y88 and height maybe 253 max but content compact 200, align-self center. It should fit.

Wait the grid row2 is 1fr and panel align-self center. Panel max-height 65dvh=253.5. With content ~200, panel height 200, centered in row2 (from 51 to 382 => center 216, panel y~116-316). Good.

Also portrait `.select-panel` uses grid-template-columns 1fr auto; fix minmax. Let's patch.

